<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 December, from 1154 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1154">1154 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">872 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry II is crowned king of England at Westminster Abbey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry II, the first Plantagenet king, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>. His lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, Normandy, Anjou and, through his wife Eleanor, Aquitaine were later called the Angevin Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1490">1490 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">536 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne of Brittany marries Maximilian I by proxy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne, Duchess of Brittany since 1488, was married by proxy to Maximilian I, King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. She went on to marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france">Charles VIII of France</a> in 1491 and Louis XII in 1499, twice becoming queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany">Anne of Brittany</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor">Maximilian I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1562">1562 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">464 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholics and Huguenots clash at Dreux</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a> was fought at Dreux, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. Both armies' commanders were captured, and the bloody outcome showed the war would be long.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1675">1675 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">351 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New England militia defeat the Narragansett in the Great Swamp Fight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-philips-war">King Philip's War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> colonial militia, with 150 Pequot allies, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narragansett-people">Narragansett people</a> near Kingston, Rhode Island, inflicting a huge number of casualties, including many hundreds of women and children. It is also called the Great Swamp Massacre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-philips-war">King Philip's War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington's army goes into winter quarters at Valley Forge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 12,000 Continental soldiers marched into camp at Valley Forge, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. Some 2,000 died of disease over the winter, but drilling under Baron von Steuben made the survivors a more effective army.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Siege of Toulon ends as the British abandon the city</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French artillery under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> forced the British to abandon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulon">Toulon</a>, ending the Republic's siege of the port, held by Royalists aided by the First Coalition. The recapture secured southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from invasion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1843">1843 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">183 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Dickens publishes A Christmas Carol</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-dickens">Charles Dickens</a>'s novella about the miser Ebenezer Scrooge went on sale and sold out its first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> by Christmas Eve. It shaped Victorian ideals of a charitable, family-centred Christmas.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The House impeaches President Clinton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US House of Representatives impeached Bill Clinton for perjury and obstruction of justice related to the Monica Lewinsky affair. The Senate acquitted him in February 1999.</p></div></li></ol>
